GRT002 rows end to end. live/app declares: a config_path to a directory
that does not exist; one to a module-only directory (main.tf, no
terragrunt.hcl); skip_outputs = true on a missing target (still fires:
Terragrunt refuses the dependency regardless); a dependencies paths entry
to a missing directory next to one to a real unit. Silent: a non-literal
config_path (unresolved) and enabled = false. config_path = "" on a block
is unresolved like a non-literal one (Terragrunt v1.1.6: "config_path could
not be resolved", no cycle): no edge, no missing-target or cycle finding.
A dependencies paths entry "" is different: it resolves to live/app itself,
a self-loop (Terragrunt v1.1.6: "cycle detected during queue
construction"). No GRT001: no outputs are read.
-- live/target/terragrunt.hcl --
inputs = {}
-- live/target/main.tf --
output "out" {
  value = 1
}
-- live/modonly/main.tf --
output "out" {
  value = 1
}
-- live/app/terragrunt.hcl --
dependency "gone" {
  config_path = "../gone"
}

dependency "modonly" {
  config_path = "../modonly"
}

dependency "skipped" {
  config_path  = "../gone_skip"
  skip_outputs = true
}

dependency "dynamic" {
  config_path = get_env("GRUNTLED_GOLDEN_NOT_SET", "../gone_dyn")
}

dependency "off" {
  config_path = "../gone_off"
  enabled     = false
}

dependency "empty" {
  config_path = ""
}

dependencies {
  paths = ["../target", "../gone_path", ""]
}

inputs = {}
-- _golden/exit --
1
-- _golden/want --
